WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.608 --> 00:00:14.971
PE!" Briana began doing warm-up stretches.

2
00:00:16.212 --> 00:00:18.354
"I wonder what we'll do today," Ally said.

3
00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:22.877
It had been too snowy for the past month to hold PE outside.

4
00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:24.779
"I don't care.

5
00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.022
Anything is better than history class," Briana said.

6
00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:30.764
"It's so boring!"

7
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:38.004
Mrs. Farrow, the PE teacher, entered the gymnasium carrying two large trash cans and a soccer ball.

8
00:00:42.047 --> 00:00:43.508
"Are we playing soccer inside?"

9
00:00:43.928 --> 00:00:45.049
Miguel asked hopefully.

10
00:00:45.069 --> 00:00:49.351
"That doesn't explain the trash cans," Briana said.

11
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.353
Mrs. Farrow grinned.

12
00:00:52.373 --> 00:00:55.375
"We are having a history lesson!"

13
00:00:55.395 --> 00:00:59.118
"No! Not history!"

14
00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:01.279
Briana moaned.

15
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:04.977
Mrs. Farrow ignored the complaint.

16
00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:11.040
"It was a snowy winter in Massachusetts in 1891," she began.

17
00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:14.222
"Too snowy for baseball or football.

18
00:01:15.403 --> 00:01:21.706
A group of college students was stuck inside for every PE class, so their teacher invented a new

19
00:01:21.786 --> 00:01:22.767
game for them to play.

20
00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:26.429
Today we're going to play that game!"

21
00:01:26.449 --> 00:01:31.772
"This might be better than regular history class," Briana thought.

22
00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:36.826
"The teacher's name was James Naismith," Mrs.

23
00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:37.447
Farrow said.

24
00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:42.851
"He based his idea on a throwing game from his childhood in Canada.

25
00:01:44.372 --> 00:01:49.095
The targets he decided on were peach baskets, but these are the best I can do."

26
00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.138
She gestured to the trash cans.

27
00:01:52.158 --> 00:01:55.300
"Now, to get them in place."

28
00:01:56.581 --> 00:02:00.404
The custodian brought a ladder and fastened a trash can high on the gym wall.

29
00:02:02.592 --> 00:02:03.933
The kids laughed at the sight.

30
00:02:07.855 --> 00:02:11.317
As the custodian put another trash can on the opposite wall, Mrs.

31
00:02:11.377 --> 00:02:13.678
Farrow divided the students into teams of nine.

32
00:02:13.698 --> 00:02:20.722
"The point of the game is to get the ball into your opposing team's trash can," Mrs.

33
00:02:20.782 --> 00:02:21.583
Farrow explained.

34
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:26.085
"You cannot run with the ball or touch the other players.

35
00:02:27.486 --> 00:02:30.068
Whichever team scores the most goals wins."

36
00:02:31.352 --> 00:02:33.593
"That sounds like basketball," Briana said.

37
00:02:33.613 --> 00:02:36.453
"Exactly!" Mrs.

38
00:02:36.493 --> 00:02:37.094
Farrow said.

39
00:02:37.114 --> 00:02:40.855
"But why do you have a soccer ball?"

40
00:02:41.215 --> 00:02:41.795
Ally asked.

41
00:02:41.815 --> 00:02:47.556
"Early basketball players used soccer balls," the teacher answered.

42
00:02:47.576 --> 00:02:52.218
"Real basketballs weren't made until 1894.

43
00:02:53.658 --> 00:02:55.799
They were made from leather and stitched together."

44
00:02:57.039 --> 00:02:58.159
She patted the soccer ball.

45
00:02:58.179 --> 00:03:01.992
"Ready for the tip-off?"

46
00:03:02.012 --> 00:03:03.654
Briana faced off against Miguel.

47
00:03:04.775 --> 00:03:09.119
Basketball was her favorite game, but she never thought it had any connection to history!

48
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.584
The teacher tossed the ball high, and both kids leaped for it.

49
00:03:14.765 --> 00:03:17.868
Briana made contact first, sending the ball straight to Ally.

50
00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:20.190
Ally dribbled—tweet!

51
00:03:21.251 --> 00:03:22.072
The whistle sounded.

52
00:03:27.424 --> 00:03:31.786
"I forgot to mention dribbling the ball wasn't allowed until 1909," Mrs.

53
00:03:31.847 --> 00:03:32.387
Farrow said.

54
00:03:32.407 --> 00:03:36.289
"The only way to move the ball is to pass it to someone else."

55
00:03:39.651 --> 00:03:40.511
They started again.

56
00:03:41.092 --> 00:03:45.814
Briana caught a pass from Kevin, the soccer ball feeling strangely soft and light in her hands.

57
00:03:46.695 --> 00:03:48.336
She shot the ball over Miguel's head.

58
00:03:49.436 --> 00:03:50.977
It clanged into the trash can.

59
00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:53.178
Ally gave her a high five.

60
00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:56.120
"You're better at history than you thought!"

61
00:03:58.156 --> 00:03:58.876
"First goal!"

62
00:03:59.237 --> 00:04:00.057
Mrs. Farrow said.

63
00:04:00.077 --> 00:04:09.122
"Now we just need to get the ball back The players waited while the teacher climbed the ladder

64
00:04:09.162 --> 00:04:10.143
and retrieved the ball.

65
00:04:10.163 --> 00:04:12.724
"Don't make too many goals!"

66
00:04:13.064 --> 00:04:13.805
the teacher joked.

67
00:04:13.825 --> 00:04:19.908
"Real baskets are definitely better than trash cans—or peach baskets!"

68
00:04:20.228 --> 00:04:20.909
Briana said.

69
00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.492
After another fifteen minutes, Miguel's team was in the lead by one goal.

70
00:04:27.712 --> 00:04:30.673
Mrs. Farrow blew her whistle again to signal the end of play.

71
00:04:30.693 --> 00:04:35.454
"Whew!" Briana was breathing hard but grinning.

72
00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.655
"That was a good game."

73
00:04:38.975 --> 00:04:40.696
Mrs. Farrow gathered the class together.

74
00:04:40.716 --> 00:04:43.856
"What do you think of old-school basketball?"

75
00:04:45.077 --> 00:04:47.577
"It's hard not to dribble the ball," Miguel said.

76
00:04:47.597 --> 00:04:52.179
"And it's strange to have more than five on a team," Ally added.

77
00:04:52.199 --> 00:04:56.260
"A lot is the same though," Briana said.

78
00:04:57.972 --> 00:05:04.457
"Making baskets, passing the ball, not touching the other players The teacher nodded.

79
00:05:04.477 --> 00:05:11.123
"Mr. Naismith wanted to make a game that was all about skill and strategy, not force."

80
00:05:12.424 --> 00:05:13.365
Briana smiled.

81
00:05:14.506 --> 00:05:16.567
"I still prefer modern basketball.

82
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:18.369
But the old-school game was fun."

83
00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:21.551
"Does that mean you like history now?"

84
00:05:21.992 --> 00:05:22.952
Mrs. Farrow asked.

85
00:05:24.073 --> 00:05:24.914
Briana laughed.

86
00:05:26.315 --> 00:05:27.096
"Not exactly!"
